Animations and transition effects:


- Animations are a very nice addition to an application. It’s not the first thing you do, of course,
    but it can really improve the user experience.

- 🔥Angular doesn’t offer much regarding animations and transitions. It assumes that you will use
    plain CSS to define them. But animating the removal of an element in pure CSS is not the easiest
    thing to do, so Angular offers some help in that area. And to be symmetric, it also offers some
    help to animate the appearance of an element.

        ⚠️Angular had a @angular/animations package for a long time that covered much
        more than the support for animating the appearance and removal of elements. But
        this package doesn’t rely on CSS, which makes it quite inefficient. It is now
        deprecated since v20.2.